Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:21:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/57] Z 6III: the still's capture job ends -- the upper
 unit's +0x14 at the still's frame end

With z63-still-capture, a release now completes the front end's capture
job: 0x422D0001 (units 0x401e, posted by sub_4102C770) ends, the front
end gets 0x41D0001 (sub_410B05A8) as its flag 0x4000, and the capture
service gets the RAW-done event 0x40F0009 (DC08 bit 1).

The job ends only on job flag 1, which the 0x106 ISR's callback
sub_40CAE2EC raises for +0x204 bit 6 when the upper unit's +0x10 or
+0x14 bit 0 is set (sub_40CAD5F0 -> sub_40C1F1B0, base 0x150c8000 via
the handle at 0xA03051458). The image sets those two bits in exactly one
place, the upper's configuration slot +40 (sub_40C1DF50 from
sub_40CAD020/278). For live view that slot comes from a per-mode table at
0x47e80000 + 0x66f0 (sub_411712C8, index map at +0x58f0): resource 0x5f
of SNOR_USER, which this image's SNOR_USER holds only in part -- the
table and its index map are zeros, so both bits are always written 0.
The capture job's own upper configuration is empty. So the still's frame
end now also sets +0x14 bit 0; the next configuration of the upper
writes it again. DECLARED: that the still's frame end marks a capture's
frame, in place of the missing parameter.

Where the still stops now. After 0x40F0009 the capture service waits for
the image-available event 0x40F0004, which the front end sends only when
its still job 0x422D0003 ends with live view stopped (sub_41020C74, case
0x41D0004). That job is posted only on the development path: the ready
combination 0x34C04 (sub_40F749EC -> sub_40F7A058 -> 0x40F7B930 ->
sub_4102DE1C), entered from the release controller's stage 32
(sub_40FBB958 -> sub_40F5EB4C, CFEC state 1), or the 0x206E path
(sub_4102E1B0, sub_40F68510). Both need at least one image output:
sub_40F79248 asks sub_40EAE230 for outputs 0..5 of the capture's image
configuration (the 62 items of 0xA02B5BB10, copied to 0xA03D7C62C), and
every output is refused. Output 0 needs item 0x2750 == 3 (sub_40EADE38),
0x2750 being the shooting-condition mirror of item 0x2A01 (index 69 of
0xA0293C218, field 0xA03D53264); the others need the 18-byte maps
0x2B01/0x2B03 (all 0xff). Item 0x274F, the output gate of sub_40EAE42C,
is status 0x4000040D: byte 0 of the sensor module's frame record
(0xA03625F18, from 0xA03625E30 = live-view object +0x35C == 1, i.e. the
capture parameter +6976 < 2). Here +6976 = 2 because the readout type
(+2380, sub_410B4580) is 2: it needs 0x2A01 == 3, or 0x2038 in {2, 3}
with 0x3607 == 1. 0x2A01 is written by nothing in this run but the
settings defaults (sub_410074E4); the release mask 0xA03D82254 (item
0x274E) follows the outputs and is 0, so stage 32 is skipped. Changing
image quality, or resetting the photo shooting menu, from the menu
changes none of these.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
